{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Rachel stole the terafim.</b> It says in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer: What are terafim? They would slaughter a firstborn human, cut it up, salt it with salt and spices, and write upon a plate of gold the name of an impure spirit, and place it under its tongue, and put it in the wall, and light a lamp before it, and bow down to it — and it would speak, as it is written: ״התרפים דברו און״. And therefore she stole them, so that they would not tell Laban that Jacob had fled. Alternatively, she intended to uproot idolatry from her father's house."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:22.862127673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}